@page "/"

<PageTitle>Home</PageTitle>

<h1 class="display-4">API Key Authentication via Pipeline</h1>
<h2 class="display-6">Workflows: Blazor client and ASP.NET Core API exchange authenticated requests using an API key</h2>

<div class="container my-4">
    <div class="jumbotron bg-light p-5 rounded">

        <div class="card shadow-sm border-0">
            <div class="card-body">
                <div class="row g-3">

                    <div class="col-md-6">
                        <div class="p-3 border bg-white rounded h-100">
                            <h5 class="text-primary"><strong>1.IHttpClientFactory</strong></h5>
                            <p class="text-muted mb-0">
                                Web client <code>CreateClient("ApiClient")</code> configured with
                               <strong><code>.AddHttpMessageHandler(someHandler)</code></strong>
                               <br>
                               <code>here : someHandler = ApiKeyDelegatingHandler </code>
                            </p>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="col-md-6">
                        <div class="p-3 border bg-white rounded h-100">
                            <h5 class="text-primary"><strong>2.Delegating Handler Adds API Key</strong></h5>
                            <p class="text-muted mb-0">
                                Before the request leaves the client,
                                <code>ApiKeyDelegatingHandler.SendAsync()</code> injects API key:
                                <br />
                                <code>X-API-KEY: &lt;client key&gt;</code>
                            </p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
 
                    <div class="col-md-6">
                        <div class="p-3 border bg-white rounded h-100">
                            <h5 class="text-primary"><strong>3.Web API Filter Pipeline</strong></h5>
                            <p class="text-muted mb-0">
                                The pipeline <code> ApiKeyAuthFilter()</code> is registered by AddScoped() in Web Api before startup.
                                ApiKeyAuthFilter<code>.OnActionExecutionAsync()</code> will check <code>X-API-KEY: &lt;client key&gt;</code> before the controller runs:
                                <ul>
                                    <li>If header missing → <strong>401 Unauthorized</strong></li>
                                    <li>If header present but incorrect → <strong>401 Unauthorized</strong></li>
                                    <li>If header matches server key → filter calls <code>next()</code> and controller executes</li>
                                </ul>
                            </p>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="col-md-6">
                        <div class="p-3 border bg-white rounded h-100">
                            <h5 class="text-primary"><strong>4.Response Returned</strong></h5>
                            <p class="text-muted mb-0">Controller returns data, HttpClient receives it, and the Blazor component renders the UI.</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
